**who —** MAGNAVOX ODYSSEY — an exereunesis sphere — the teardown

**what —** The first home video game console had no CPU, no software, and no sound. Ralph Baer's machine drew a few movable white dots with discrete transistor-diode logic, and you taped translucent plastic overlays onto your TV for the 'graphics' and colour. Primitive beyond modern imagining — and the start of everything.

**where —** the teardown — a made machine, opened and explored  Framework inputs: the chips; the buses; the spec; the lore  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)

**why —** The first home video game console had no CPU, no software, and no sound. Ralph Baer's machine drew a few movable white dots with discrete transistor-diode logic, and you taped translucent plastic overlays onto your TV for the 'graphics' and colour. Primitive beyond modern imagining — and the start of everything.

